    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Ref # Kanzen Master Level 1 - p67 - no.62",
      "html": "<b>Ref #</b> Kanzen Master Level 1 - p67 - no.62",
      "credits_raw": "LR",
      "content_sha256": "82f81643f6588481f86bef957fb7b3cb53441768ef22f7f8c4ea97a551a1bf63",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "NOUN + 〜にそくして / 〜にそくした",
      "html": "NOUN + 〜にそくして / 〜にそくした",
      "credits_raw": "LR",
      "content_sha256": "227b83c123d269d8896770b5b7c8eab4b93e81d659cd68a2b6815f15899d64df",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "You do realize that this phrase is rather formal and used mostly in written material.",
      "html": "You do realize that this phrase is rather formal and used mostly in written material.",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "04a6e26e2df0f4ff164d282032f91d482be15c362cd7816ac63d29d2e0c3f9b3",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "i had no idea, so it will be noted!",
      "html": "i had no idea, so it will be noted!",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "66c9252a274b3b375f9eba512960ca89b91135ddfedca288e6b382adfc693ba6",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "perhaps [nisotte] is a similar but less formal phrase?",
      "html": "perhaps [nisotte] is a similar but less formal phrase?",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "d818e20a891738e6f43cfee9c051ebff2352bee8c1469218c71cbd84cd40b293",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Yes, it is. にしたがって（従う） is not as casual as にそって（沿う） and is also not formal as に即して。に従って and に沿って are used in conversation as well.",
      "html": "Yes, it is. にしたがって（従う） is not as casual as にそって（沿う） and is also not formal as に即して。に従って and に沿って are used in conversation as well.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "ceb12f0f3ad9a06b0709962b27ec42202562a9e576ed6fc174575e67c64185e8",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I thought に従って [nishitagatte] implied more hierarchy, or cause and effect, whereas [nisotte] is more in parallel?\n\n(fact) [nishitagatte] (effect)\n\n高い。従って、買わなかった\nIt was expensive. Accordingly, I did not buy it.\n\n川に沿って道\nthe street parallel with the river",
      "html": "I thought に従って [nishitagatte] implied more hierarchy, or cause and effect, whereas [nisotte] is more in parallel?<br/><br/>(fact) [nishitagatte] (effect)<br/><br/>高い。従って、買わなかった<br/>It was expensive. Accordingly, I did not buy it.<br/><br/>川に沿って道<br/>the street parallel with the river",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "023fb44295ac12859fbc6eb15e055f3520cb06d5c5b448546fc31989e0b9eb2c",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Your 従って in the eg above is 接続詞 conjunction. \nMy 従って is a transformation of 従う。Yes, 従う implies hierarchy but not all the time. Also 沿う and 従う aren't the same meaning but implications are the same here. \nexample :\nPlease answer following the example\n例題に即して、回答してください。\n例題に沿って、回答してください。\n例題に従って、回答してください。",
      "html": "Your 従って in the eg above is 接続詞 conjunction. <br/>My 従って is a transformation of 従う。Yes, 従う implies hierarchy but not all the time. Also 沿う and 従う aren't the same meaning but implications are the same here. <br/>example :<br/>Please answer following the example<br/>例題に即して、回答してください。<br/>例題に沿って、回答してください。<br/>例題に従って、回答してください。",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "4a7a095e02aff2896b4c577c789446d0d828726b0d6653c77dc7254cc147ece4",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "See also に即した \"based on, adapted to\"\nプロとして現実に即した解決策を提示します。\nAs professionals we present solutions adapted to the facts of the situation.",
      "html": "See also に即した \"based on, adapted to\"<br/>プロとして現実に即した解決策を提示します。<br/>As professionals we present solutions adapted to the facts of the situation.",
      "credits_raw": "Paul",
      "content_sha256": "946d8402641d12cea580b8bbf75162efd59a4780a820416a7e9abc99346aa42e",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "According to two of my texts, this phrase is written using different 漢字 depending on the nuance: に即して (in accordance with the facts, objective reality, experience, etc.) and に則して (in accordance with arbitrary rules, laws, etc.) Following that, #5151 is not written correctly (boo to ALC). However, I also see that another source uses に即して in both cases, so maybe this is just a nitpicky distinction. Can any native speakers address this?",
      "html": "According to two of my texts, this phrase is written using different 漢字 depending on the nuance: に即して (in accordance with the facts, objective reality, experience, etc.) and に則して (in accordance with arbitrary rules, laws, etc.) Following that, #5151 is not written correctly (boo to ALC). However, I also see that another source uses に即して in both cases, so maybe this is just a nitpicky distinction. Can any native speakers address this?",
      "credits_raw": "srobertson",
      "content_sha256": "b9bdf5f4ad80efa320d8434b77c7a9b5aba80644d683bcbe3b860ae856458640",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 11,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "In Kanzen master it says 即 is appropriate for things that conform to experience or a situation, and 則 is for when things conform to laws and rules.",
      "html": "In Kanzen master it says 即 is appropriate for things that conform to experience or a situation, and 則 is for when things conform to laws and rules.",
      "credits_raw": "LR",
      "content_sha256": "61085ceeeb382247518316a7e551edf12c515b3f4338a85a3dc329c6b7f82c56",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
  ],
